    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9558" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντεισ-φέρω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>contribute in return,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς εἰσφοράς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					654
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ τυχόντα ἔρανον ἀλλήλαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					<u>UP</u>
					8.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμον ἀ.</span>
			<i>substitute a new</i> law <i>for</i> an old one, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				20.97
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καινὰ δαιμόνια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					52.36
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>introduce as a countor measure,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				42.12
			</span></i>.</div>
